2.5 Unauthorised borrowing will be charged at the Bank's standard unauthorised rate, details of which are available on request.

**3. REPAYMENT AND CANCELLATION**

3.1 The facility is repayable on demand at any time.

3.2 The facility is granted for a period of 12 months from 1 May 2023, subject to annual review.

3.3 The Bank may cancel or reduce the facility at any time by written notice, in which case all outstanding amounts become immediately due and payable.

**4. SECURITY**

4.1 The facility is secured by a fixed and floating charge over the assets of Ellison Bookkeeping Services Ltd, registered at Companies House on 15 June 2015 (charge no. 08911234).

4.2 A personal guarantee from yourself, limited to £10,000, is held in respect of this facility. The guarantee is dated 29 April 2022 and remains in full force and effect.

4.3 No additional security is required in connection with this renewal.

**5. COVENANTS**

5.1 You undertake to provide to the Bank, within 90 days of each financial year end:

(a) Annual audited financial statements for Ellison Bookkeeping Services Ltd;

(b) A copy of the company's Corporation Tax computation and return as submitted to HMRC.

5.2 You undertake to provide quarterly management accounts within 30 days of each quarter end. These may be provided in a summary format agreed with your Relationship Manager.

5.3 You undertake to notify the Bank immediately in writing of:

(a) Any material adverse change in the financial condition of the company;

(b) Any change in the nature of the business;

Heston Bank has overdraft limit 20000 GBP. Record status: current.

(c) Any legal proceedings threatened or commenced against the company;

(d) Any change of directors or shareholders holding more than 25% of the issued share capital.

5.4 The company will not, without the Bank's prior written consent, create or permit to subsist any security over its assets other than the security referred to in clause 4.

**6. REPORTING AND INFORMATION**

6.1 You will provide the Bank with such financial or other information as the Bank may reasonably request from time to time.

6.2 The Bank may carry out a review of the facility at any time, including a review of the company's banking records, books and accounts.

6.3 You will promptly provide the Bank with any information which you become aware of that could reasonably be expected to affect the Bank's decision to continue providing the facility.

**7. EVENTS OF DEFAULT**

7.1 The Bank may demand immediate repayment of all amounts outstanding and/or cancel the facility if any of the following events occur:

(a) You fail to pay any amount due under this facility on the due date;

(b) You breach any covenant or undertaking set out in this letter and fail to remedy such breach within 14 days of notice from the Bank;

(c) Any information provided to the Bank in connection with this facility is found to be misleading or incorrect in any material respect;

(d) Any security becomes invalid or unenforceable, or the Bank reasonably considers that the value of the security has diminished or been put at risk;

(e) A petition is presented or an order made for the winding up of the company, or the company passes a resolution for voluntary winding up;

(f) A receiver, administrator or administrative receiver is appointed over any part of the company's assets;

(g) The company ceases to carry on business or threatens to do so;

(h) You, as guarantor, die or become incapable of managing your affairs, or a petition is presented for your bankruptcy;

(i) Any other event occurs which, in the Bank's reasonable opinion, materially impairs the company's ability to perform its obligations under this facility.
